# This file sets a stable line end for each text file. Git detects a text
# file and normalizes it to LF in the repository (`text=auto`). A shell
# script and gradlew keep LF. A Windows batch file keeps CRLF. A PowerShell
# script stays text, with the normal `text=auto` conversion. A JAR, a PNG,
# and an ICO file stay binary, with no conversion.
* text=auto

*.sh text eol=lf
/gradlew text eol=lf
/gradlew.bat text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text

*.jar binary
/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary

# Git keeps the LF line end of the pre-commit hook. The hook is a POSIX
# shell script and needs LF, also on a Windows clone.
/.githooks/pre-commit text eol=lf
